243: - Host limits recorded as feature-matrix rows (D7; each row carries its P0.2 receipt; none adds a mechanism): (1) Stop-gate enforcement: classic cline has no Stop-equivalent hook in this table, so the Stop gate never runs there and its host sessions end only by the 12-hour idle rule; cline-v2 `afterRun` and opencode `session.idle` fire after the model has stopped, so the gate evaluates and reports but cannot hold the run open, and a Stop that leaves turns open records `stop_gate_overridden_by_host` (inference from the hook timing; P0.2 records each host's behavior). (2) Per-tool audit: the tool audit the TypeScript hosts run today (cline-v2 `beforeTool` and `afterTool`, `mcpserver-cline-v2-plugin/src/plugin.ts:250-275` at `e776d94`; opencode `tool.execute.before` and `.after`, `mcpserver-opencode-plugin/src/plugin.ts:226-254` at `36ed34d`) is not forwarded, because the PowerShell core has no tool-audit hook (`plugins/core/lib-ps/plugin-hook.ps1:5` at `a8d3934b`), so those hosts match the PowerShell hosts; a tool audit stays with QB-AGENT-001's `tool_execution` work (C6). (3) Required memories (FR-MCP-MEMORY-007): forwarded on cline-v2 (`beforeModel`) and opencode (`chat.message` `output`) as above; classic cline's stdio entry attaches the block to request-boundary tool results today (`withRequiredMemoryInjection`, `mcpserver-cline-plugin/src/index.ts:89` at `7909599`), which the logic-free entry no longer does, so its native UserPromptSubmit PowerShell hook returns the block as the hook's `context_modification` output (`apps/vscode/proto/cline/hooks.proto:37-41` in the local Cline source at `b090c4a08`); where P0.2 shows that context does not reach the model, the row records the limitation with the explicit memory-list fallback FR-MCP-MEMORY-007 allows.
