251: - C2 Server-minted turn identity (alias journal: A3/A5 own it in the PowerShell cache, the only plugin cache since the 2026-10-11 PowerShell-only ruling, and A8 keeps committed aliases durably discoverable to every registered consumer through the PowerShell consumer interface (QB-AGENT-001's outbox among them once its PowerShell form exists; the operator decided the port on 2026-10-12, R2-F10, and Codex's ACK of the 2026-10-12 CONTRACT entry is the open item), which reapplies them idempotently until it has durably applied them (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001-AC008); its observable contract is FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001-AC008, and its interface is locked in TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008 AC-007): requestIds come from the mint route (D1); an event recorded before the mint returns carries the turn's `ingressNonce` and the provisional `pending-<nonce>` id. The move from `pending-<nonce>` to the minted requestId is the single explicit exception to requestId immutability and never changes the logical owning turn: the alias (old id, new id, `aliasedAtUtc`) is journaled atomically before any event is rewritten, every bound event is rebound in original order (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001-AC008), readers resolve either id through the alias journal's permanent lookup entry, which is never pruned (only the consumer-delivery obligation is retired once every required consumer acknowledges), and restart and replay reapply a journaled alias without minting again.
252: - C3 Turn outcomes and event persistence receipts stay separate (TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008 AC-006). Turn outcomes (server per turn: `created`, `merged`, `skipped_terminal`; no `skipped_duplicate`, removed by the operator on 2026-10-09) are owned by this plan; event receipts (eventId, payloadHash, committed revision) by QB-AGENT-001. On a persistence path with an audit outbox (QB-AGENT-001's; its governed-host protections move to the PowerShell core in A8 under R2-F10, and the rest of its Node work awaits Codex's ACK of the 2026-10-12 CONTRACT entry): `created` and `merged` (including reason `no_change`) count as persisted only when the event identity, hash, and committed revision match; `outcomeVerified:false` (server without per-turn outcomes) never satisfies a mandatory persistence obligation; `skipped_terminal` maps to `rejected`, is never retried or quarantined, and keeps the event and its receipt (reason, `storedStatus`) as terminal evidence, while only the plugin failsafe record is cleared.
